      "text": "Workers should look at the time‑of‑payment rule in the Omnibus Rules. It says wages must be paid at least once every two weeks or twice a month, and the interval between payments may not exceed sixteen (16) days. Because the payroll is twelve days late, it is still within the maximum interval, but the employer must still meet the sixteen‑day ceiling. If the employer cannot pay because of force‑majeure or other circumstances beyond its control, payment must be made immediately after those circumstances end.",
