      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "The manager’s claim that customers have not paid yet falls under the ‘circumstances beyond the employer’s control’ exception. The same rule permits a delay only when a force‑majeure event or similar uncontrollable circumstance exists, and even then the employer must pay the wages immediately once the event ceases. Therefore, workers can examine whether the lack of customer payments qualifies as an allowable circumstance, and if not, the employer remains bound by the regular sixteen‑day payment schedule.",
