    {
      "component_id": "concern_003",
      "text": "The overall wage‑payment framework that employees should inspect is the Section 3 provision of the Omnibus Rules. It requires wages to be paid not less than twice a month, with intervals not exceeding sixteen (16) days, unless a force‑majeure or other uncontrollable circumstance occurs, in which case payment is due immediately after the circumstance ends. For work paid by results, the same sixteen‑day interval applies proportionally, and final settlement must be made immediately upon completion of the work.",
      "evidence": [
        { "quote_id": "concern_003.s2.q1" },
        { "quote_id": "concern_003.s2.q2" }
      ]
