      "text": "Workers should look to the time‑of‑payment rule, which says wages must be paid at least once every two weeks or twice a month, and the interval between payments cannot exceed sixteen days. If wages are paid by results for work that cannot be finished in two weeks, the same sixteen‑day maximum applies, with final settlement made as soon as the work is completed.",
