      "text": "An employer may delay payment only when a force‑majeure event or circumstances beyond its control occur; in such cases the employer must pay the wages immediately after the event or circumstance ends. The manager’s claim that customers have not paid does not fall within this statutory exception, so the regular sixteen‑day payment schedule still applies.",
