      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Where an employer’s business normally allows deductions for loss or damage, a wage deduction is only permitted if (a) the employee is clearly shown to be responsible, (b) the employee is given a reasonable chance to explain why the deduction should not be made, (c) the amount is fair, reasonable and does not exceed the actual loss, and (d) the deduction does not exceed 20 % of the employee’s weekly wages. If any of these conditions are not met, the deduction is unlawful.",
      "evidence": [
