      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "For a regular holiday, Art. 94 of the Labor Code requires that every worker be paid his regular daily wage, unless the employer is a retail or service establishment that regularly employs fewer than ten workers; the rule also does not apply to government employees, domestic helpers, managerial staff, or unsupervised field personnel. Thus, an ordinary private shop that does not fall within those exclusions must pay the day's wage even if it stays closed.",
