      ]
    },
    {
      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Under the Omnibus Rules (Section 5) and Art. 295, an employment is deemed regular when the employee performs activities that are usually necessary or desirable in the employer’s usual business, except when the job is fixed for a specific project or is seasonal; any employment not covered by that description is classified as casual, although an employee who has rendered at least one year of service—continuous or broken—shall be considered regular with respect to that activity.",
