{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Where the statutory conditions are met, an employment is deemed regular if the worker is engaged to perform activities that are usually necessary or desirable in the employer’s usual business or trade, unless the work is fixed for a specific project whose completion was determined at hiring or is seasonal and limited to that season. If those conditions are not met, the job is casual, but any employee who has rendered at least one year of service, continuous or broken, is considered regular with respect to that activity and continues while the activity exists.",
