      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "The regular‑employment test says a worker is regular when he is hired to do activities that are usually necessary or desirable in the employer’s ordinary business, unless the job is for a specific project whose end was set when he was hired or is seasonal and limited to that season. Even if those conditions are not met, anyone who has rendered at least one year of service, whether continuous or broken, is treated as regular for that activity.",
