      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "Under the Labor Code, “employer” means any person or entity acting directly or indirectly in the interest of an employer, including private firms, while “employee” covers any individual employed by such an employer. “Employment” is defined as remunerative work performed for an employer. These definitions provide the basic framework for private employment relationships.",
