      "component_id": "concern_001",
      "text": "Where the statutory conditions are met, the authorized‑cause framework for termination is that an employer may dismiss only for the just causes listed in Article 283 of the Labor Code; termination for a just cause does not automatically grant termination pay, though other benefits under contracts or policies may still apply. The cited provision does not set out any specific notice period or procedural notice requirement for such dismissals.",
