      "text": "When a consumer buys a product from a retailer, the retailer is subsidiarily liable under the warranty if both the manufacturer and distributor fail to honor it; the retailer must shoulder the expenses needed to honor the warranty. The buyer can enforce the warranty simply by presenting the warranty card or receipt to the retailer, with no other documentary requirement. The warrantor must remedy the defect within a reasonable time and without charge, and after reasonable attempts the consumer may elect a refund or replacement, though the refund is not guaranteed to be immediate.",
