      "text": "A consumer who bought a defective fan can file a complaint with the DTI by submitting a petition or a letter‑complaint. The department logs the complaint and may start an investigation. The consumer arbitration officer then schedules a hearing, giving both parties notice of the date, time and place and attaching a copy of the complaint. The officer first tries to settle the dispute; if settlement fails, a formal investigation and hearing proceed. The case must be decided within fifteen days after the investigation ends.",
