      "component_id": "concern_002",
      "text": "If the item you received is not what you ordered and the mistake is not your fault, the Consumer Act as applied by JAO 24‑03 and RA 11967 gives you the right to demand repair, replacement, or a refund. When you choose replacement or refund, the e‑retailer may require the return of the wrongly delivered goods at no cost to you, and the return must be made within a reasonable period after you receive the notice, unless you and the merchant agree otherwise.",
